# What ThreadSanitizer reports that isn't HIRAKU's (tools/sanitize.sh thread): libraries that
# aren't built with it, whose own locks and atomics it can't see.
#
# Mesa's OpenGL: its driver thread and the caller share hash tables and its own allocator's blocks
# under locks of its own (tests/picture: 67 reports, every one with both sides inside libgallium)
called_from_lib:libgallium
race:libgallium

# libdbus (the request for real-time threads at a window's start, the lights' and readers' own):
# its connection and its message queue each have a lock, taken in either order by the one thread
# that uses it here
deadlock:libdbus

# ==== Only for the tests that paint (tools/sanitize.sh: $paint); the other tests stop above ====
# Qt's raster painter: a big fill (QPainter on a QImage or QPixmap: the launcher's switches and
# game cards, tests/launcher/test_theme and test_gamecards) is split over Qt's own pool of paint
# threads (qdrawhelper.cpp blend_color_argb and handleSpans, QThreadPool and its QRunnables). The
# pool hands the work over and back with QMutex and QSemaphore, on Linux bare futexes that
# ThreadSanitizer can't see: the runnables' new and delete, the pool's list of its threads
# (QArrayData) and the picture's pixels (memcpy) show as races. Seen with Arch's Qt debug files
# (2026-11-18): every report's both sides are in QThreadPoolThread::run, QThreadPoolPrivate,
# QRunnable's QGenericRunnable or qdrawhelper.cpp, and no HIRAKU code runs off the main thread in
# these two tests. Those names can't be the lines: without debug files (this PC's CachyOS Qt, the
# runner's Qt Company Qt) those frames have no name, only their library, so the lines name the
# library; what keeps them narrow is that only those two tests read them.
race:libQt6Core
race:libQt6Gui
# The pool, a global, joins its idle threads only after main has returned: a thread leak, and a
# race on a QWaitCondition's destruction (the latter matched above). QThread::start is exported
# (named with or without debug files); HIRAKU starts no QThread of its own.
thread:QThread::start
